\ The raise from eager_tail_boundary_compiled_caller.1z with `boom`'s effect declared, pinned
\ eager. Both sides of the boundary now compile, and each adds a row the interpreted chain in
\ tail_boundary_compiled_caller.1z does not carry.
\
\ The compiled `go` reaches `when` through its fallback boundary, which pends the `when` row. The
\ `if` inside `when` runs the arm inline, and the compiled `boom` there raises rather than being
\ tail-called, so the `if` frame is pended too. The interpreted chain is the target.

boom: ( -- ) [ f "kaboom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;
go: ( ? -- ) [ [ boom ] when ] ;

[ t go ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
